  "details": "This is a huge oversight on the part of VR Chat, I believe. We need to be able to unbind the touch sensors. It's creating a lot of jittery hand movement, when pressing the button does the same action anyway. \n\nIt's best if this can be made user-set as well\n\nFor example, touching the trigger or grip button does the same hand gesture and fully pressing them down. \n\nTouching the analogue sticks or jump button on its own does a peace sign, even when moving the stick or jumping by fully pressing the button! \n\nPersonally, I'd keep all the gestures on a full press, though keep the peace sign on touching the blank area on the controllers.\n\nAgain, it's easier if this can just be set by the user. If we just had these as options, this wouldn't be an issue.",
